Z||000013||contra||09-24-2000||10:37 PM||||personally though<BR>i think within the next year<BR>i'm going to remove my chin spoiler<BR>you wont believe how much it scrapes going out of driveways and parking lots<BR>and my car isn't even lowered! =/<P>i'm going to remove it, then repaint my front fascia, and then drop my car a couple inches. the stock fascia has an angle in the front curving up which when my car is lowered will give me the angle i need to get down steep hills with no trouble.<P>i'm sure anybody with a spoiler on the front has scraped their's enough times now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||sluppy123||09-24-2000||11:14 PM||||The Chin spoiler on the GT is from RSM. I paid around  $150 US. I always had problems with it being to low to the ground, Now I have lowering springs installed and it's imposible to drive with it on. It's now being put on another car.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=6751238&p=23380894&Sequence=0"> <P>If I was to buy another one, I'd buy it from IRM. I have a IRM chin on my 85' SC and it's built alot better than the RSM one.(more re-enforcement at the leading edge) It's been on the car for 5 years with no problems.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=1843822&p=16438930&Sequence=0"> <P><P>------------------<BR>-Brian S.<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT||||reg||1
